From 2a3c2d16855859e03960ba962eda10e7d1aab1f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: adbtrr_work5 <adbtrr_work5@local>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 14:05:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] mm/heapinfo: add timed capture window with allocation
 backtrace

Adds heap leak detection over a bounded time window, plus the allocation
call-stack needed to trace a leak candidate back to its origin.

Allocation backtrace
 - sched_backtrace() (lib/libc/sched) returns the call stack of the current
   thread by walking the compiler generated EHABI unwind tables through
   libgcc's _Unwind_Backtrace.  No frame pointer, no stack scan heuristic and
   no syscall trap.
 - Heap nodes carry the immediate malloc caller plus HEAPINFO_BACKTRACE_DEPTH-1
   deeper frames, recorded on the allocation path for user space allocations.
 - Toolchain support: -funwind-tables for the code being unwound.

Capture window
 - "heapinfo -c start" arms a window on the selected heap, "heapinfo -c stop"
   disarms it and reports, in three sections: blocks allocated during the
   window and still alive, pre window blocks resized inside it with their old
   and new size, and pre window blocks freed inside it.
 - The table is maintained on the same code path that updates the per pid
   heapinfo counter, so the reported totals reconcile with the counter delta
   rather than being derived from a separate heap walk.
 - Capture state lives in struct mm_heap_s so the kernel side ioctl can arm a
   window that the user side allocator observes in a protected build.  The
   table is allocated from the target heap only while a window is active.
 - heapinfo_add_size()/heapinfo_subtract_size()/heapinfo_update_node() take
   the node and the heap so the table can be updated in step with the counter.

Kernel and allocator side only; the heapinfo command line options that drive
this are a separate commit.
